=== Diffie-Hellman   p = 23, g = 5 ===
  Alice      secret x = 6, sends A = g^x mod p = 5^6 mod 23 = 8
  Bob        secret y = 15, sends B = g^y mod p = 5^15 mod 23 = 19
  Alice      K = B^x mod p = 19^6 mod 23 = 2
  Bob        K = A^y mod p = 8^15 mod 23 = 2
  => shared key K = g^(xy) mod p = 2 (both sides agree)
  - Eve sees p = 23, g = 5, A = 8, B = 19; getting K needs a discrete log
  - plain DH is unauthenticated, so a man in the middle can run one exchange with each side
